  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Principle
    
    Slide Prism splits aurora-light through crystalline conductors into narrow, controllable beams that refract across ice and water, rendering visible the bioluminescent trails krill leave in their blooms. A harvester holds the prism steady — one flipper locked, breathing shallow — while the light bends through successive angles, mapping migration patterns no unaided eye could track. The technique permits krill harvesting at scales that were, prior to its refinement, not possible.
    
    ## Development and Practitioners
    
    The technique was refined at the Beacon Stack during the Clever Ice Age by E'frostlings engineers, who discovered that aurora-charged lenses could be calibrated to follow krill movements across vast stretches of frozen sea. Dedicated Slide Prism refineries still operate on the Stack's harvester platforms.
    
    The practice is unforgiving. Miscalibrated prisms shatter the user's vision permanently, in ways no fire-healer has been able to mend. Even successful practitioners accumulate geometric crystalline scars across their flippers — burn marks from sustained crystal-conduction that deepen with mastery, not failure. Among documented practitioners: Beacon-Keeper Lianhinglou, who learned forbidden techniques combining aurora-light with deep-pressure methods in the ☽'dwell Teneanemus~ chamber beneath Wane Oncea; Lianhingme hi'Shard; Light-Regents Lianoshing and Xouhoulong; and Grand Auditor Mingmeyang, whose current deterioration may bear some relation to the practice's cumulative toll, though the chronicles are careful not to say so directly.
    
    The technique spread beyond E'frostlings to the Aureate merchant guilds, the Midnight Claws syndicate, the Icebound Exchange, and Holdborn (ice-thresh) harvesters desperate to feed their colonies during the Long Dark.
    
    ## Weaponization and the Slaughter Moon
    
    When the Orca Incursion struck the harvesting fleets, the krill-blooms became killing grounds — a catastrophe the records call Slaughter Moon. The efficiency that fed colonies also concentrated them in predictable locations. Orca shamanics adapted Slide Prism techniques during the Shattered-Spire Assault to breach the Aurora Stack's eastern ridge and its inner crystal barriers, turning a harvesting tool into a siege weapon.
    
    The claim that abundance itself drew the raids deserves more scrutiny than it typically receives.
    
    ## Political Consolidation
    
    Following E'frostlings' territorial victories — including the seizure of the Veil Vents from the fallen Holdborn faction — the technique became a political instrument. E'frostlings consolidated control over most prism-trained harvesters, binding food security to factional loyalty.
    
    Ledger-Warden Shumei ehua'Frost still practices it.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771576006984_0", anchor: "The claim that abundance itself drew the raids deserves more scrutiny than it typically receives.", text: "I left this sentence deliberately undercooked. Here is what the deep ice actually shows: the \"vast stretches of frozen sea\" that Slide Prism opened to industrial harvesting overlap almost exactly with orca pod feeding territories documented in Wake-Singer pressure-songs preserved at Scar☽ Lucamlinaecius. Krill-bloom migration routes are not secrets — orcas had tracked them for generations before any penguin pointed a prism at the water. Abundance did not draw the raids. Encroachment provoked them. At least two of the assaults attributed to the Incursion's opening phase match the retaliatory pattern perfectly: targeted strikes against harvesting platforms occupying traditional hunting grounds. The preferred narrative — mindless predation against innocent industry — requires ignoring everything the ice recorded about what was there before we were.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771576006984_1", anchor: "Orca shamanics adapted Slide Prism techniques during the Shattered-Spire Assault", text: "\"Adapted\" implies they learned the technique. They did not. Orcas lack the anatomy for sustained crystal-conduction and have no access to aurora-charged lenses. What the eastern ridge ice-memory preserves is pressure-song harmonics shattering crystalline barriers at resonant frequencies that correspond to prismatic refraction angles. The Wake-Singers did not adopt our tool. They watched us use it long enough to identify what it made brittle, then broke it with their own magic. That is not adaptation. That is intelligence work.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771576006984_2", anchor: "though the chronicles are careful not to say so directly", text: "Because Mingmeyang is still Grand Auditor. Chroniclers develop exquisite caution around figures who can audit their funding.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
